# nltest.tech -- the minimal technology of the NETLIST golden cases whose inputs are
# hand-written .ext files (tests/golden/NETLIST/CASES.md; m7-extraction design D21, task 2.5).
#
# ext2spice and ext2sim read the device types, their source/drain/substrate resistance
# classes and the default substrate names from the current extract style (ExtGetDevInfo,
# ext2spice.c:932, ext2sim.c:647). Every .ext input says `tech nltest` and `style nltest`,
# so the style matches (EFread.c:529-600) and area/perimeter values are written. Resistance
# classes: 0 diffusion (1000), 1 poly (5000), 2 metal1 (100): node records carry three
# area/perimeter pairs. tools/golden/authoring/netlist_cases.py replaces the device lines
# when a row needs other default substrate names (NL-SPICE-08, NL-SPICE-14).
tech
    format 35
    nltest
end

planes
    well
    active
    metal1
    metal2
end

types
    well    pwell,pw
    well    nwell,nw
    active  ndiff,nd
    active  pdiff,pd
    active  nfet
    active  pfet
    active  poly,p
    active  rpoly
    active  npn
    metal1  metal1,m1
    metal2  metal2,m2
    metal2  mimcap
end

contact
end

styles
    styletype mos
end

compose
end

connect
    poly    nfet,pfet
end

cifoutput
end

cifinput
end

drc
end

extract
style nltest
    cscale 1
    lambda 1
    step 100
    sidehalo 0
    planeorder well 0
    planeorder active 1
    planeorder metal1 2
    planeorder metal2 3
    resist ndiff,pdiff 1000
    resist poly 5000
    resist metal1 100
    areacap metal2 1
    device mosfet nfet nfet ndiff pwell,space GND!
    device mosfet pfet pfet pdiff nwell VDD!
    device resistor rppd rpoly poly
    device capacitor mimcapm mimcap metal1
    device diode dn ndiff pwell
    device bjt npn npn ndiff pwell
end
